tg wrote:

> But if you have two scrolls with the same buc status with the same name
> then they will have similar effects.
> 
> This is assuming, of course, that you haven't changed the names of
> individual scrolls using #name.

If you change the name of a *class* of scrolls, you get "a scroll called
identify" instead of "a scroll labeled PRIRUTSENIE" (for instance) for
every scroll of that type.

If you change the name of an individual scroll, it keeps its type name: "a
scroll labeled PRIRUTSENIE called cursed".

It's impossible to change the name of an *individual* scroll so that you
can't recognise it.

